## Step 10: Update tests

Key test scenarios:
- Config loads agents from BUILTIN_AGENTS (not JSON)
- agent_for_phase handles string format (backward compat)
- agent_for_phase handles object format with model
- Empty string/null/missing model all result in no model flag
- Unknown agent names in agent_for_phase fall back to default (not raise)
- Migration removes `agents` key
- Migration always removes `current_agent` (whether or not `default_agent` exists)
- Migration resets unknown agent names to "default" while preserving model
- Migration wrapped in try/except doesn't crash on errors
- CLI `set-model` and `clear-model` work correctly
- Model flag injection in runner command building is at end for BOTH claude and opencode
- TUI loads both old and new format correctly via PhaseConfig normalization

## Scope exclusions (explicit)
- **Custom agent definitions are out of scope.** Only built-in agents (claude, opencode) are supported. Users cannot define new agents. If new agents are needed, they are added to BUILTIN_AGENTS in the Python code.
- **Model name validation is not performed.** Invalid model names are passed through to the agent, which will report its own error.

